# Copy to .env for local development. Never commit .env.
#
# Configuration keys nest with a double underscore: Email:MailerSend:ApiToken
# is Email__MailerSend__ApiToken.

# ── Email ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Leave the whole section unset for local development. A Development host with
# no provider configured captures messages to the console — links included —
# and delivers nothing, so the application runs with no credentials at all.
#
# Outside Development, a missing provider or a missing credential stops the
# application at startup rather than letting it run and drop mail silently.
# See src/Sw5e.Email/README.md for every key.

# MailerSend | Smtp | Capture
#Email__Provider=MailerSend
#Email__FromAddress=noreply@example.com
#Email__FromName=SW5e
#Email__ReplyToAddress=support@example.com

# SECRET. Issued per sending domain in the MailerSend dashboard. Never commit a
# real value here or anywhere else.
#Email__MailerSend__ApiToken=

# Generic SMTP relay, used when Email__Provider=Smtp. Port 587 with STARTTLS;
# port 465 is not supported and is rejected at startup.
#Email__Smtp__Host=smtp.example.com
#Email__Smtp__Port=587
#Email__Smtp__UserName=
# SECRET. Same rules as the API token.
#Email__Smtp__Password=

# ── Accounts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The API refuses to start without an identity connection string: an API that
# boots happily with no account system is one serving an unauthenticated site
# without saying so. Identity may have its own least-privileged role, with
# rights over nothing but the `identity` schema, or share the platform one.
#
# SECRET once a password is filled in. Same rules as every other credential
# here: never commit a real value.
ConnectionStrings__Sw5eIdentity=Host=localhost;Port=5432;Database=sw5e;Username=sw5e;Password=

# Where emailed verification and recovery links point. Configured rather than
# derived from the request: deriving it would let anyone who can set a Host
# header decide where an account recovery link goes.
Identity__PublicSiteUrl=http://localhost:5173

# The registrable domain passkeys are bound to — a bare domain, no scheme, no
# port, no path. Leave it unset for local development so the framework uses the
# request's own host; set it in every deployed environment. Changing it
# invalidates every passkey already registered.
#Identity__RelyingPartyId=sw5e.example

# Exact origins the browser application is served from, compared exactly. Leave
# unset when the site and the API share a hostname behind the reverse proxy,
# which is the common and safest case.
#Identity__AllowedOrigins__0=https://sw5e.example

# Applies migrations and seeds the roles during startup. Convenient locally;
# off in production, where migrations are a deliberate separate step.
Identity__InitializeDatabaseAtStartup=true

# Promoted to administrator on the next start, if an account with this address
# exists. Creates nothing: the person registers through the ordinary public
# flow and proves control of the address like anybody else.
#Identity__BootstrapAdministratorEmail=you@example.com

# ── Content ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#Content__RootPath=../../../sw5e-database/content
